From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 03:51:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ask: core kernel fields and hooks for the fast path

The core kernel side of the ASK fast-path stack on LS1046A. The SDK
drivers' side -- the FMan EHASH classifier extensions and the DPAA hooks
cdx registers -- is in ASK's SDK copy, sdk/linux.

Declares the master CONFIG_CPE_FAST_PATH Kconfig in net/Kconfig and
extends the core kernel with the skb fields (iif_index, ipsec_offload)
and the net_device field (wifi_offload_dev) that later patches consume:
__netif_receive_skb_core() records the ifindex a frame arrived on, GRO's
skb reuse clears it, and the skb header copy carries ipsec_offload.
validate_xmit_skb() does not linearize a frame for an offloaded SA, and
skb_scrub_packet() keeps such a frame's extensions: the DPAA driver reads
its secpath to find the SA's SEC queue after a PPPoE or tunnel device has
scrubbed it.

dev_get_stats() adds the offloaded interfaces' counters through a hook
cdx registers (dev_fp_stats_get_register()). Its deregister clears the
pointer and synchronize_rcu()s before returning, so cdx deinit can free
module text safely and a later load can register again; readers take a
READ_ONCE snapshot.

rtnetlink reports a route's MTU metric from its dst when the route sets
none, usbnet reserves 64 bytes of fast-path headroom, and
include/linux/fsl_oh_port.h declares the offline-port lookup the SDK's
OH port driver exports. MAX_LINKS in UAPI rises from 32 to 64; the Wi-Fi
driver opens its socket at MAX_LINKS - 1. The top Makefile takes
SUBDIRS= as M= for out-of-tree module builds.

Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
